SDK GPU: synchronise primary ring buffer re-init with the command processor worker.
Phase B item B1 (docs/sdk-from-source.md, docs/boot-hang-20261008.md). Applied by
tools/build_sdk_from_source.py to the runtime tree (rexgpu-xenos), and the same hunks
are appended to backends/metal/sdk-metal.patch for the Metal plugin, which compiles
command_processor.cpp itself. InitializeRingBuffer reset only the read index, on the
guest thread, unsynchronised with WorkerThreadMain, so the worker replayed
ring[0, old write index): duplicate GPU frame callbacks in ~95% of Fable II boots and
a rare endless frame-throttle spin. Now it drains the worker (read == write), parks it
with the 0xBAADF00D sentinel, resets both indices (CP_RB_WPTR = 0) and lets the guest's
next write pointer update run only the new packets (bounded 50 ms wait; on a timeout
the old behaviour). The worker publishes the read index last and reads it between two
loads of the write index, so the reset can never pair with a stale write index.
Cvar gpu_ring_reinit_sync (default true) turns the synchronisation off for A/B tests.
The executable's __imp__VdInitializeRingBuffer override asks the plugin
(fable2_ring_reinit op 2) and stands down while this is active.

